export const services=[
['water-heaters','Water Heaters','COMFORT, RESTORED','Hot water.\nWithout the uncertainty.','A cold shower, a leaking tank, or water that runs hot and cold deserves a closer look. Understand the issue before deciding on repair or replacement.','home',
[['Start with the symptoms','Tell us when the problem began, whether the entire home is affected, and if you have noticed water near the heater. Keep model information handy if safely accessible.'],['Repair or replace?','Equipment age, tank condition, repair history, and household demand all matter. A leaking connection and a leaking storage tank call for different solutions. Assessment comes before recommendation.'],['Plan the installation','A replacement must fit demand, fuel source, space, venting, and connections. Ask about suitable equipment. Tankless installation availability needs direct confirmation.'],['Maintenance matters','Follow manufacturer instructions for your model. Ask about inspection and maintenance, especially if noise, output, or temperature has changed.']],
[['Does every leak mean replacement?','A connection may be repairable. A deteriorated storage tank is a different issue. Have the source assessed before choosing equipment.'],['Should I choose a larger tank?','Demand, space, recovery rate, and installation requirements matter. Discuss household use before choosing capacity.']],
'What changed with your hot water?',[['No hot water','Note whether every fixture is affected and whether the change was sudden. Call with the model if accessible.'],['Water near the tank','Avoid electrical components. Connection leaks and tank leaks need different responses; call for assessment.'],['Planning replacement','Compare demand, installation requirements, maintenance, and suitable equipment options.']]],
['drain-clearing','Drain Clearing','GET THINGS MOVING','A clear drain.\nA better day.','Standing water and recurring clogs interrupt everyday life. Find the source of the restriction instead of living with another temporary fix.','kitchen',
[['One fixture or the whole house?','A single slow sink may point to a local blockage. Several affected fixtures can suggest a restriction farther along the drainage system. Share which drains are affected.'],['Kitchen and bathroom blockages','Grease and food residue restrict kitchen drainage. Hair, soap buildup, and objects obstruct bathroom drains. Line location and condition guide the clearing method.'],['When the clog comes back','Repeated blockages deserve investigation. Ask whether a camera inspection could help locate buildup, roots, or damage rather than repeating the same process.']],
[['Should I keep running water into a backed-up sink?','Stop using the fixture so water does not overflow. Call to discuss symptoms and next steps.'],['Why does the same drain keep clogging?','Recurring clogs can reflect buildup, an object, or an issue farther along the line. Clearing and inspection address different parts of diagnosis.']],
'Compare drainage symptoms',[['One slow fixture','A local restriction may be involved. Note whether it occurs only during use of that fixture.'],['Several slow drains','A restriction farther along may be involved. Stop use if wastewater is backing up.'],['Recurring blockage','Ask whether camera inspection could help explain a repeated problem after clearing.']]],
['leak-detection','Leak Detection','FIND THE SOURCE','Small clues.\nClearer answers.','A rising water bill, a damp patch, or water sounds when fixtures are off can point to a hidden leak. Investigate before committing to repair.','home',
[['Follow the evidence','Note where you first noticed moisture, when it appears, and whether it changes when a fixture runs. Photos and bills help describe intermittent issues.'],['Walls, fixtures, and foundations','A wet surface is not always the source. Water can travel along framing or pipes. Investigation distinguishes fixtures, supply lines, and possible leaks beneath a slab.'],['Detection before repair','Once a likely source is identified, discuss access, repair options, and the affected pipe. An opening or repair should follow an explanation of findings.']],
[['Does a high bill prove there is a leak?','No. Irrigation, use, and billing periods also affect consumption. An unexplained change warrants investigation.'],['Does every hidden leak require opening a wall?','Access depends on location and findings. Discuss proposed access before work proceeds.']],
'Where are you noticing a clue?',[['Near a fixture','Look only at accessible surfaces. Note whether moisture appears during use or remains afterward.'],['Along a wall','Staining may be separated from the source. Photograph the area and note when it appeared.'],['At the floor','Warm or damp flooring has several causes. Arrange investigation rather than assuming a slab leak.']]],
['water-filtration','Water Filtration Systems','A THOUGHTFUL APPROACH TO WATER','Choose filtration\nfor your home.','Start with the water concern you want to address. A system should fit your supply, intended use, and maintenance needs.','kitchen',
[['Define the concern','Taste, odor, sediment, and contaminants are different concerns. Review quality information or appropriate testing before selecting equipment. No filter addresses everything.'],['At the sink or throughout the home','Under-sink equipment treats one outlet. Whole-home equipment treats incoming water. Placement, flow, and service access affect selection.'],['Keep maintenance in the plan','Cartridges and media need replacement at manufacturer intervals. Ask about costs and access before installation.']],
[['Will a filter remove every contaminant?','No. Performance depends on the model, certifications, and substances it reduces. Match equipment to a documented need.'],['Is filtration the same as softening?','No. They address different concerns. Discuss which approach fits your water and goals.']],
'Where do you want treated water?',[['At one sink','Supply → selected under-sink system → compatible outlet. Consider space and cartridge access.'],['Whole home','Incoming supply → whole-home equipment → distribution. Confirm flow capacity and the treatment goal.'],['Not sure','Start with water-quality information. Choose equipment for a documented need.']]],
['plumbing-repairs','Plumbing Repairs','THE EVERYDAY, TAKEN CARE OF','Let’s get your\nplumbing working.','From a leaking connection to a fixture that will not shut off, the right repair starts with understanding what failed and why.','bathroom',
[['Describe the change','Sudden or gradual? One fixture or several? Pressure, noise, temperature, and moisture help narrow investigation.'],['Connections, pipes, and fixtures','Repair may involve a valve, fitting, pipe, or fixture component. Understand the affected part and proposed work before proceeding.'],['When it cannot wait','Active flooding, uncontrolled leaks, and wastewater backups warrant a call. Stop using affected fixtures and avoid water near electrical equipment.']],
[['Can I send photos before a visit?','Call or email photos of accessible areas. Do not dismantle equipment or enter unsafe areas for photographs.'],['What should I report about low pressure?','Note whether it affects hot, cold, or both and whether other fixtures have the issue.']],
'Start with what you notice.',[['Visible leak','Describe location and how quickly water appears. Call directly for uncontrolled water.'],['Low pressure','Compare hot and cold water and affected fixtures. Local restrictions and whole-home issues need different investigation.'],['A fixture won’t stop','Describe continuous flow, repeated refilling, or a control that will not close.']]],
['new-construction-plumbing','New Construction Plumbing','BUILD ON A BETTER PLAN','Good plumbing\nstarts on paper.','Thoughtful planning connects the rough-in work you cannot see with the fixtures you use every day. Start the conversation before walls close.','home',
[['01 / Plan the system','Discuss fixtures, demand, supply, drainage, venting, and equipment access. Share plans and construction milestones.'],['02 / Coordinate rough-in','Routes must work alongside framing and other trades. Coordinate penetrations, connections, and inspection stages.'],['03 / Finish and test','Fixture installation follows rough-in and finished surfaces. Testing and applicable inspections check connections and operation.']],
[['When should a plumber review plans?','Early coordination identifies routing and access before framing and finishes limit options.'],['What information should I provide?','Plans, fixture schedules, location, project phase, and timeline. Scope and availability are confirmed directly.']],
'Explore the project sequence.',[['Planning','Fixture schedule → supply demand → routing and access → coordination.'],['Rough-in','Set supply, waste, and vent routes; coordinate framing and inspections.'],['Completion','Connect fixtures, test operation, and coordinate final inspections where required.']]],
['faucets-and-fixtures','Faucets & Fixtures','THE DETAILS YOU USE EVERY DAY','Better fixtures.\nBetter everyday living.','A dripping faucet or dated fixture can be a practical repair or a chance to improve your space. Get help with fit, connections, and installation.','kitchen',
[['Repair the drip','Worn components, loose connections, and damaged bodies cause different leaks. Identify the source before deciding whether repair is practical.'],['Choose for the installation','Sink openings, mounting, connections, clearance, and finish matter. Check compatibility before purchasing.'],['Finish with the details','Check connections, operate controls, and look for leaks after installation. Keep manufacturer information for parts and maintenance.']],
[['Can you install a fixture I purchased?','Contact DLR with the model and installation details to confirm scope and compatibility.'],['Does every dripping faucet need replacing?','Some can be repaired. Replacement may make sense when parts are unavailable or the body is damaged.']],
'Choose a fixture setting.',[['Kitchen','Check openings, spout reach, sprayer clearance, shutoffs, and cabinet connections.'],['Bathroom','Consider mounting, basin dimensions, reach, finish, and supply access.'],['Utility','Consider use, accessories, and the surrounding work area.']]],
['repiping-and-pipe-repairs','Re-Pipes & Pipe Repairs','CARE FOR THE SYSTEM BEHIND THE WALLS','A stronger plan\nfor aging pipes.','Repeated leaks and corroded connections deserve a system-level conversation. Compare focused repair with replacement of affected piping.','home',
[['A repair with a clear scope','An isolated damaged section may suit local repair. Surrounding condition helps establish how far work should extend.'],['When a broader approach makes sense','Frequent leaks, widespread corrosion, and ongoing pressure concerns justify evaluation. These signs alone do not establish that a full repipe is necessary.'],['Understand access and materials','Discuss materials, routes, shutoffs, wall access, and finish restoration before approving a scope. Different properties need different plans.']],
[['Does an old home automatically need repiping?','No. Condition, materials, failure history, and assessment matter more than age.'],['What should a repiping discussion cover?','Areas replaced, materials, permits, interruptions, access, and restoration responsibilities.']],
'Compare the scope of work.',[['Focused repair','Addresses an identified section. Ask about surrounding condition and recurring problems.'],['Partial replacement','Replaces a branch or area. Clarify retained connections and access.'],['Whole-home evaluation','A broader recommendation should be based on actual condition and findings.']]],
['bathroom-and-kitchen-plumbing','Toilets, Sinks, Showers & Tubs','THE MOST-USED ROOMS IN YOUR HOME','Make every\nfixture work.','A running toilet, slow sink, or leaking shower affects the household. Take care of connections that keep kitchens and bathrooms useful.','bathroom',
[['Toilets and sinks','Running toilets may involve tank components; base moisture needs different investigation. Sink issues may involve faucets, valves, traps, or drains.'],['Showers and tubs','Leaks, temperature changes, and control issues can originate at valves or connections. Explain when issues occur and other affected fixtures.'],['Replacement and installation','Dimensions, drain position, supply, and access influence choices. Coordinate with cabinetry, tile, and finish work.']],
[['Why does my toilet keep refilling?','An internal seal or other tank component may need attention. Inspection establishes the cause.'],['Can you help with a bathroom remodel?','Discuss fixtures, connections, access, and construction scheduling before installation.']],
'Explore a fixture.',[['Toilet','Supply → fill mechanism → bowl and waste connection. Running water and base leaks need different checks.'],['Sink','Supply → faucet → basin → trap and drain. Note where moisture appears.'],['Shower & tub','Mixing valve → outlet; separate waste and overflow. Describe leaks or temperature changes.']]],
['sewer-camera-inspections','Camera Inspections','SEE BEFORE YOU DECIDE','A closer look\ninside the line.','A sewer camera helps assess accessible drain and sewer piping. Images inform repair discussions when recurring problems need explanation.','home',
[['What the camera reveals','Buildup, roots, cracks, and changes in condition may be visible where travel and visibility permit. Cameras do not see through walls or every obstruction.'],['Access and visibility matter','Suitable access is needed. Standing water or blockage can limit the view; clearing may be needed first.'],['Findings into next steps','Ask what was observed, where, and how it relates to symptoms. Inspection does not automatically mean whole-line replacement.']],
[['Can inspection find every problem?','No. Access, configuration, water, and blockage limit the view. Discuss limitations.'],['Is inspection the same as clearing?','No. Cameras inspect visible conditions; clearing removes obstructions. Either or both may be appropriate.']],
'Understand an inspection finding.',[['Buildup','Wall buildup can restrict flow. Findings inform clearing and maintenance.'],['Roots','Roots can enter openings or joints. Discuss removal and the condition allowing entry.'],['Damage','A crack or displacement needs context. Ask about location, access, and repair options.']]],
['custom-plumbing-solutions','Custom Plumbing Solutions','YOUR PROJECT, THOUGHT THROUGH','An unusual space.\nA considered solution.','Renovations and unusual layouts call for more than a standard answer. Start with the constraints, then develop a practical scope.','home',
[['Share the goal','Explain the change and what is not working. Plans, photos, selections, and access make discussion productive.'],['Resolve the constraints','Supply, drainage slope, venting, structural access, and clearances influence what can be built. Coordinate with other trades.'],['Agree on a path forward','Clarify inclusions, open decisions, and findings that could change the plan. A documented scope makes complexity easier to understand.']],
[['Can you assess a nonstandard installation?','Contact DLR with location and goals to confirm whether the project fits its scope.'],['Do I need finished plans to call?','No. Early discussion identifies needed information. Proposals may require plans and assessment.']],
'Build a useful project brief.',[['The goal','Describe the change, space, use, and selections.'],['The constraints','List access limitations, connections, construction stages, and trades.'],['The next step','Contact DLR about scope and availability. A site assessment may be needed.']]]
].map(([slug,name,tag,h1,intro,image,sections,faq,toolTitle,choices])=>({slug,name,tag,h1,intro,image,sections,faq,toolTitle,choices}));


